    <item>
      <title>Documentation</title>
      <link>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/employability/learning/documentation/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://curriculum.codeyourfuture.io/guides/employability/learning/documentation/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;If you have not taken the &lt;a&#xA;  href=&#34;https://developers.google.com/tech-writing/one&#34;&gt;Technical Writing course&lt;/a&gt;, do so now.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are three key aspects of technical writing for developers:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;code&#34;&gt;Code&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your code should be simple, clearly named, and easy to follow. Your code must express your ideas, not encrypt them.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;comments&#34;&gt;Comments&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Why, not what&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Your comments should explain why you&amp;rsquo;ve made a choice, not what the code does. Your code should be simple, clearly named, and easy to follow, and if it isn&amp;rsquo;t, refactor it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Exercism</title>
